1
00:00:00,875 --> 00:00:03,083
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:09,166 --> 00:00:11,583
[Ras coughing]

3
00:00:11,583 --> 00:00:13,208
Clear your mind,

4
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:14,875
then begin.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,875
Do I hear celebration pies?

6
00:00:19,875 --> 00:00:21,500
[together] Oh, pies!

7
00:00:24,541 --> 00:00:26,166
-[all talking excitedly]
-Oh, those smell so good.

8
00:00:27,041 --> 00:00:27,916
[gobbling]

9
00:00:33,791 --> 00:00:37,250
What are you waiting for?

10
00:00:37,250 --> 00:00:38,208
Go!

11
00:00:49,291 --> 00:00:50,250
Now...

12
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,375
transfer Spinjitzu momentum

13
00:00:52,375 --> 00:00:53,916
to one of the stones.

14
00:00:59,791 --> 00:01:00,833
[growling]

15
00:01:00,833 --> 00:01:02,500
Another failure!

16
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:07,000
I see mental conflict in you.

17
00:01:08,208 --> 00:01:09,208
It's nothing.

18
00:01:09,208 --> 00:01:10,166
I'll try again.

19
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:12,458
You're thinking
about the Ninja.

20
00:01:12,458 --> 00:01:14,916
Forget those cowards and fools.

21
00:01:14,916 --> 00:01:16,541
They're not cowards.

22
00:01:16,541 --> 00:01:18,291
They might have made
some mistakes,

23
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:19,583
but they're heroes.

24
00:01:19,583 --> 00:01:21,416
"Hero"?

25
00:01:21,416 --> 00:01:23,458
That word is meaningless.

26
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:25,625
To some, I'm a hero.

27
00:01:25,625 --> 00:01:26,750
[coughing]

28
00:01:26,750 --> 00:01:28,083
It's easy to be a hero

29
00:01:28,083 --> 00:01:29,916
to those who agree with you,

30
00:01:29,916 --> 00:01:32,458
and a villain
to those who don't.

31
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:34,625
But the Ninja
have saved the world.

32
00:01:34,625 --> 00:01:35,625
[growling]

33
00:01:35,625 --> 00:01:38,291
They didn't save mine!

34
00:01:38,291 --> 00:01:39,125
[coughing]

35
00:01:39,125 --> 00:01:40,166
No one did!

36
00:01:40,166 --> 00:01:42,708
You've never told me
what happened--

37
00:01:42,708 --> 00:01:45,291
And they didn't save
your parents.

38
00:01:46,708 --> 00:01:48,625
I blame Master Wu for that.

39
00:01:48,625 --> 00:01:50,750
As you should.

40
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:53,708
[coughing]

41
00:01:53,708 --> 00:01:55,125
[gasping in pain]

42
00:01:55,125 --> 00:01:56,625
You're weak.

43
00:01:56,625 --> 00:01:59,333
I am injured, not weak.

44
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:01,208
Never mistake the two.

45
00:02:01,208 --> 00:02:02,416
But you're getting worse.

46
00:02:02,416 --> 00:02:04,750
Yes.

47
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:05,958
[wincing]

48
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:07,416
I am dying...

49
00:02:07,416 --> 00:02:08,958
[gasping]

50
00:02:08,958 --> 00:02:10,208
and with me,

51
00:02:10,208 --> 00:02:13,166
your chances
of finding your parents.

52
00:02:14,625 --> 00:02:15,750
Our only hope

53
00:02:15,750 --> 00:02:19,041
is deep inside
the Spectral Lands.

54
00:02:20,916 --> 00:02:24,000
We must continue on.

55
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,041
What even are
the Spectral Lands?

56
00:02:27,041 --> 00:02:29,208
They are dark lands

57
00:02:29,208 --> 00:02:32,291
for those that are
no longer living.

58
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:38,708
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

59
00:02:38,708 --> 00:02:41,666
♪ Together we will rise ♪

60
00:02:41,666 --> 00:02:45,166
♪ We fight ♪

61
00:02:45,166 --> 00:02:48,250
♪ Be a ninja
for what's right ♪

62
00:02:51,166 --> 00:02:53,458
[♪♪♪]

63
00:02:53,458 --> 00:02:55,333
So, no rumors
on your travels

64
00:02:55,333 --> 00:02:57,333
of a certain Ninja
that shoots lightning

65
00:02:57,333 --> 00:02:58,500
and makes bad jokes?

66
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,166
No, but in the Endless Sea,

67
00:03:00,166 --> 00:03:02,625
I did get shocked
by an electric eel.

68
00:03:02,625 --> 00:03:04,041
Does that help you?

69
00:03:07,166 --> 00:03:09,208
[Nya] I can't believe
it's come to this...

70
00:03:09,208 --> 00:03:10,875
asking randos in the street

71
00:03:10,875 --> 00:03:12,958
where the love of my life
could be.

72
00:03:12,958 --> 00:03:14,791
What else can we try?

73
00:03:14,791 --> 00:03:17,541
We've been all over the place
and found nothing.

74
00:03:17,541 --> 00:03:20,875
Jay's better at disappearing
than Mr. Pale.

75
00:03:20,875 --> 00:03:23,041
Maybe we don't need
to find Jay.

76
00:03:23,041 --> 00:03:26,000
Maybe we just bring Jay to us.

77
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,166
Sure, brilliant!

78
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:28,916
Oh, except how?

79
00:03:28,916 --> 00:03:31,708
You wanna attract lightning,
you put up a lightning rod,

80
00:03:31,708 --> 00:03:34,666
and that's our lightning rod.

81
00:03:34,666 --> 00:03:38,500
[Nya] "Grand opening
of Lobbo's Totally Rad Arcade,

82
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:39,791
Lobbo-Lobbo"?

83
00:03:39,791 --> 00:03:41,208
That guy will throw his money

84
00:03:41,208 --> 00:03:43,250
into any terrible business idea.

85
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:45,916
Lobbo's Arcade has
a Galamorph X-Post cabinet.

86
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:47,333
Eh? Eh?

87
00:03:48,291 --> 00:03:49,375
[sighing]

88
00:03:49,375 --> 00:03:51,500
There was a GX-P
in Ed and Edna's junkyard

89
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:52,666
where Jay grew up.

90
00:03:52,666 --> 00:03:54,541
He was speed-running it
since he was a kid,

91
00:03:54,541 --> 00:03:56,916
and is still
the high-score record holder.

92
00:03:56,916 --> 00:03:57,958
It's his favorite game!

93
00:03:59,166 --> 00:04:00,291
So?

94
00:04:00,291 --> 00:04:01,791
So get this--

95
00:04:01,791 --> 00:04:04,125
I've been practicing GX-P
on an emulator.

96
00:04:04,125 --> 00:04:06,875
I think I've got the skills
to finally beat his high score,

97
00:04:06,875 --> 00:04:08,041
and if that happens,

98
00:04:08,041 --> 00:04:09,875
he'll come from anywhere
in the Merged Lands

99
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:11,333
to take back his top spot.

100
00:04:12,208 --> 00:04:14,541
Jay doesn't have
his memory, Kai.

101
00:04:14,541 --> 00:04:17,208
He won't remember
Gala-post-morph...

102
00:04:17,208 --> 00:04:18,708
Galamorph X-post.

103
00:04:18,708 --> 00:04:21,000
He won't even remember
it exists.

104
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,083
No matter
what's happened to Jay,

105
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:25,291
no matter
if his goodness is shattered,

106
00:04:25,291 --> 00:04:26,791
or his memory gone,

107
00:04:26,791 --> 00:04:29,083
wherever he is,
whatever he's doing,

108
00:04:29,083 --> 00:04:30,750
if his high score is broken,

109
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:33,208
he'll feel it, and he'll come.

110
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:35,666
Why would Jay be so crazy
about a video game?

111
00:04:35,666 --> 00:04:37,208
They're super boring.

112
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:40,833
All that grammar and spelling.

113
00:04:40,833 --> 00:04:42,250
I played every game

114
00:04:42,250 --> 00:04:44,375
in my Caregiver Bot's
memory banks,

115
00:04:44,375 --> 00:04:46,083
and they were all the worst.

116
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:47,625
"Carrying the one."

117
00:04:47,625 --> 00:04:49,500
"Using proper manners."

118
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:50,500
Blech!

119
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,750
Oh, Wyldfyre.

120
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:55,041
I predict this is going to be
a very big day for you.

121
00:05:00,583 --> 00:05:02,208
[grunting with effort]

122
00:05:03,916 --> 00:05:05,000
[thudding and wincing]

123
00:05:06,333 --> 00:05:09,458
[Arin grunting, Ras grumbling]

124
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:15,583
I'm guessing
that's the Spectral Lands?

125
00:05:16,625 --> 00:05:18,375
Yes.

126
00:05:19,291 --> 00:05:20,208
Hurry.

127
00:05:21,458 --> 00:05:23,541
[thudding and groaning]

128
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:25,708
I'm sorry,

129
00:05:25,708 --> 00:05:28,000
I don't think
I can get you in there safely.

130
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,291
Tell me what I need
to get for you.

131
00:05:30,291 --> 00:05:32,625
No. I-I must--

132
00:05:32,625 --> 00:05:34,875
[coughing and wheezing]

133
00:05:34,875 --> 00:05:36,500
You can't make it,

134
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,958
and we're losing time.

135
00:05:37,958 --> 00:05:39,500
Tell me what you need.

136
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,500
[Ras wheezing]

137
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:42,166
After the Merge,

138
00:05:42,166 --> 00:05:44,291
there were legends.

139
00:05:44,291 --> 00:05:46,333
I... I need...

140
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:49,166
healing elixir

141
00:05:49,166 --> 00:05:51,500
from the Well of the Lost.

142
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:53,250
Well of the Lost. Got it.

143
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,375
Any clue where it is in there?

144
00:05:57,375 --> 00:05:59,208
Village center...

145
00:05:59,208 --> 00:06:00,916
hilltop.

146
00:06:05,875 --> 00:06:07,500
Okay, you stay here.

147
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:08,833
Save your energy. I'm going in--

148
00:06:08,833 --> 00:06:11,166
Arin!

149
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:14,166
Returning Blade.

150
00:06:14,166 --> 00:06:16,375
Prismatic steel.

151
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:18,083
You...

152
00:06:18,083 --> 00:06:20,250
will need it.

153
00:06:21,166 --> 00:06:22,166
On it!

154
00:06:22,166 --> 00:06:23,500
Don't die on me, Ras.

155
00:06:31,291 --> 00:06:32,416
[shivering]

156
00:06:32,416 --> 00:06:34,291
This place is freezing.

157
00:06:38,541 --> 00:06:42,916
Okay, not seeing
any dead people... yet.

158
00:06:49,666 --> 00:06:51,000
Wow.

159
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,958
This is just...

160
00:06:52,958 --> 00:06:54,375
Wow.

161
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:55,708
Welcome, customers,

162
00:06:55,708 --> 00:07:00,666
to Lobbo's Totally Rad Arcade,
Lobbo-Lobbo!

163
00:07:00,666 --> 00:07:03,541
Home to some games
Lobbo invented,

164
00:07:03,541 --> 00:07:04,416
for example,

165
00:07:04,416 --> 00:07:06,375
Whack-a-Lobbo!

166
00:07:06,375 --> 00:07:09,750
For some reason, that's
Lobbo's mom's favorite game.

167
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:14,166
And here is the Lobbo-Roll-O!

168
00:07:14,166 --> 00:07:17,041
All completely new
and original gaming concepts,

169
00:07:17,041 --> 00:07:18,875
trademark Lobbo Industries.

170
00:07:18,875 --> 00:07:20,416
Lobbo-Lobbo.

171
00:07:20,416 --> 00:07:21,833
Wow, Lobbo.

172
00:07:21,833 --> 00:07:24,750
This is so... fun.

173
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:25,708
Is that the right word?

174
00:07:25,708 --> 00:07:26,666
Look, we're here for--

175
00:07:26,666 --> 00:07:27,708
[Lobbo] A delicious meal?

176
00:07:27,708 --> 00:07:30,375
Lobbo has you covered!

177
00:07:30,375 --> 00:07:34,416
Lobbo's world-famous
endless Casserole Pit!

178
00:07:34,416 --> 00:07:36,666
Lobbo-Lobbo!

179
00:07:36,666 --> 00:07:38,166
[belching]

180
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:43,416
Actually, we're here for
the Galamorph X-post machine.

181
00:07:43,416 --> 00:07:45,833
Ah, a retro gamer!

182
00:07:45,833 --> 00:07:47,000
Good choice!

183
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,500
Even if it could use
a Lobbo-themed update.

184
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:51,833
Lobbo-Lobbo.

185
00:07:51,833 --> 00:07:54,041
[gasping in delight]

186
00:07:54,041 --> 00:07:56,666
Hello, old friend.

187
00:07:56,666 --> 00:07:59,166
Your Kai guy is back.

188
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:00,875
Really?

189
00:08:00,875 --> 00:08:02,375
Ignore her.

190
00:08:02,375 --> 00:08:03,541
She's just jealous.

191
00:08:03,541 --> 00:08:05,375
You honestly think
this dumb plan

192
00:08:05,375 --> 00:08:07,916
has even the slightest chance
of working?

193
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:11,250
You have a better idea
we should try instead?

194
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:14,750
I wonder if they got that
"Organize your bedroom" game.

195
00:08:14,750 --> 00:08:16,458
I was pretty good at that one.

196
00:08:19,458 --> 00:08:21,125
[game music playing]

197
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:22,750
[Wyldfyre] What?

198
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:26,750
This has nothing to do
with bedroom organization.

199
00:08:26,750 --> 00:08:30,666
There's video games
where you can blast stuff?

200
00:08:30,666 --> 00:08:31,750
Wait...

201
00:08:31,750 --> 00:08:34,583
can video games be exciting?!

202
00:08:34,583 --> 00:08:35,708
[cackling in delight]

203
00:08:44,041 --> 00:08:44,958
Whoa! [gasping]

204
00:08:44,958 --> 00:08:47,125
[struggling]

205
00:08:47,666 --> 00:08:48,541
[branches creaking]

206
00:08:57,625 --> 00:08:58,500
[shutters slamming]

207
00:08:58,500 --> 00:08:59,708
[gasping] H'yah!

208
00:09:02,958 --> 00:09:03,958
[debris clattering]

209
00:09:03,958 --> 00:09:06,208
Returning Blade?

210
00:09:06,208 --> 00:09:07,333
Nice.

211
00:09:07,333 --> 00:09:09,625
Why was Ras
keeping this thing a secret?

212
00:09:11,541 --> 00:09:14,375
"Village Center, Hilltop."

213
00:09:14,375 --> 00:09:16,041
It's gotta be this way--

214
00:09:16,041 --> 00:09:17,125
Whoa!

215
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:18,708
Watch out, buddy!

216
00:09:18,708 --> 00:09:20,958
You're messing
with the wrong guy today!

217
00:09:20,958 --> 00:09:22,500
[nearby snarling]

218
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:23,458
Get down!

219
00:09:23,458 --> 00:09:25,541
[blows thudding]

220
00:09:25,541 --> 00:09:27,041
What is going on?

221
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,416
You have prismatic steel!

222
00:09:30,416 --> 00:09:31,875
Why aren't you
looking through it?

223
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:38,083
Whoa...

224
00:09:38,083 --> 00:09:39,875
[beast snarling]

225
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:45,666
[Arin gasps]

226
00:09:55,250 --> 00:09:56,125
[snarling]

227
00:09:57,583 --> 00:09:59,625
There are nodes on its back.
Strike them!

228
00:10:02,708 --> 00:10:03,625
H'ah!

229
00:10:03,625 --> 00:10:04,791
Yeah!

230
00:10:04,791 --> 00:10:08,000
Eat that,
weird invisible ugly beast!

231
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,083
Problem solved.

232
00:10:10,083 --> 00:10:11,625
Not solved.

233
00:10:11,625 --> 00:10:13,041
Why not?

234
00:10:13,041 --> 00:10:14,083
[distant snarling]

235
00:10:14,083 --> 00:10:15,958
They hunt in packs.

236
00:10:20,666 --> 00:10:22,000
[♪♪♪]

237
00:10:23,833 --> 00:10:25,208
[munching]

238
00:10:28,666 --> 00:10:30,208
[furious blasting]

239
00:10:34,125 --> 00:10:35,333
[grunting in frustration]

240
00:10:35,333 --> 00:10:36,625
[furious blasting]

241
00:10:37,958 --> 00:10:39,000
[groaning]

242
00:10:40,041 --> 00:10:41,166
[game sounds]

243
00:10:49,458 --> 00:10:51,708
[rapid beeping and blasting]

244
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:54,833
[Lobbo]
Tuna Gelatin, with mints!

245
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,083
-[yelping]
-[casserole belching]

246
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:03,541
[beeping and blasting]

247
00:11:05,125 --> 00:11:06,375
[laughing excitedly]

248
00:11:15,666 --> 00:11:17,791
[groaning in frustration]

249
00:11:19,666 --> 00:11:21,916
[distant screeching of beasts]

250
00:11:21,916 --> 00:11:23,500
I gotta get you out of here.

251
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:26,666
Soul-Suckers like draining
the spirit energy of the living

252
00:11:26,666 --> 00:11:28,000
even more than the dead.

253
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:29,791
Dead... like you?

254
00:11:29,791 --> 00:11:30,916
Of course.

255
00:11:30,916 --> 00:11:32,833
This place
is only for the Departed.

256
00:11:32,833 --> 00:11:34,750
Living people
should never come here,

257
00:11:34,750 --> 00:11:36,583
so let's go
before those things come back.

258
00:11:36,583 --> 00:11:37,791
I can't leave.

259
00:11:37,791 --> 00:11:39,000
I need something.

260
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,666
You're going to be killed!

261
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:42,833
What could you possibly need
from here?

262
00:11:42,833 --> 00:11:46,250
Elixir from something
called the "Well of the Lost."

263
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,125
[beast snarling]

264
00:11:47,125 --> 00:11:48,041
I'm a Ninja,

265
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,125
and my...

266
00:11:49,125 --> 00:11:50,791
my teacher is dying.

267
00:11:50,791 --> 00:11:53,125
I was once a Ninja,

268
00:11:53,125 --> 00:11:55,666
and I know masters
are very important.

269
00:11:55,666 --> 00:11:57,166
[beast snarling closer]

270
00:11:57,166 --> 00:11:58,708
I know where the well is.

271
00:11:58,708 --> 00:12:00,708
Keep close
if you want to stay alive.

272
00:12:05,291 --> 00:12:07,708
[snarling]

273
00:12:07,708 --> 00:12:11,166
Yeah, I'd like to stay alive.

274
00:12:11,166 --> 00:12:13,166
[beasts screeching]

275
00:12:15,833 --> 00:12:17,416
Oh, man, oh, man...

276
00:12:17,416 --> 00:12:19,125
I've never made it
to this level before.

277
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:20,500
I-- Uh-- Uh--

278
00:12:23,083 --> 00:12:23,916
[victorious beeping]

279
00:12:23,916 --> 00:12:25,666
[cheering]

280
00:12:25,666 --> 00:12:26,875
I did it! I did it!

281
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,583
Well, I finally beat you, Jay!

282
00:12:29,583 --> 00:12:30,708
[laughing]

283
00:12:30,708 --> 00:12:32,791
Time for you
to defend your high score!

284
00:12:36,166 --> 00:12:38,333
Come on,
even if this does work,

285
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:40,958
it's not like he'd be
instantly teleported to--

286
00:12:40,958 --> 00:12:41,833
[door banging open]

287
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:42,958
[gasping]

288
00:12:42,958 --> 00:12:45,333
[dove cooing]

289
00:12:48,541 --> 00:12:50,416
Oh, hey, guys!

290
00:12:50,416 --> 00:12:53,041
Uh, were you all waiting for me?

291
00:12:53,041 --> 00:12:55,166
Who are you again?

292
00:12:56,208 --> 00:12:57,875
[cooing like a dove]

293
00:13:00,875 --> 00:13:02,500
I knew this wouldn't work.

294
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:03,750
Give it time, sis.

295
00:13:03,750 --> 00:13:04,916
He'll be here.

296
00:13:04,916 --> 00:13:07,416
Maybe it'll help
if I play more games.

297
00:13:07,416 --> 00:13:09,875
Yeah, I'll do that.

298
00:13:09,875 --> 00:13:11,208
For Jay.

299
00:13:19,166 --> 00:13:20,958
[screeching]

300
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:25,791
I thought the Departed Realm

301
00:13:25,791 --> 00:13:27,708
was where everyone went
when they died.

302
00:13:27,708 --> 00:13:30,583
Why are you and those monsters
the only things here?

303
00:13:30,583 --> 00:13:32,750
Oh, the Departed Realm
was way messed up

304
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:33,916
even before the Merge

305
00:13:33,916 --> 00:13:36,500
turned it into
the Spectral Lands.

306
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:39,666
We had the Cursed Realm
end up inside here,

307
00:13:39,666 --> 00:13:41,000
so when the Merge happened,

308
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,166
both realms
got all mixed together.

309
00:13:43,166 --> 00:13:45,375
It's a mess. Let's go.

310
00:13:45,375 --> 00:13:47,083
But shouldn't there be

311
00:13:47,083 --> 00:13:49,000
more Departed Souls here
than just you?

312
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,125
After the Merge,

313
00:13:50,125 --> 00:13:52,416
the Departed were finally
able to move on.

314
00:13:52,416 --> 00:13:53,416
"Move on"?

315
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,416
To where?

316
00:13:54,416 --> 00:13:55,416
I don't know.

317
00:13:55,416 --> 00:13:57,666
Another phase of existence?

318
00:13:57,666 --> 00:13:59,083
To be reborn?

319
00:13:59,083 --> 00:14:00,375
Beats me,

320
00:14:00,375 --> 00:14:03,375
but I like to think
they go to eternal rest,

321
00:14:03,375 --> 00:14:04,666
and when people die,

322
00:14:04,666 --> 00:14:06,125
they still come here,

323
00:14:06,125 --> 00:14:07,500
but they only pass through,

324
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,541
and as they do,

325
00:14:08,541 --> 00:14:10,541
they're vulnerable
to Soul-Suckers,

326
00:14:10,541 --> 00:14:11,916
so I protect them.

327
00:14:11,916 --> 00:14:14,125
Why haven't you moved on?

328
00:14:14,125 --> 00:14:17,875
Sometimes I feel the pull
to do just that,

329
00:14:17,875 --> 00:14:20,291
but I told you, I was a Ninja,

330
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:21,833
and I've decided it's my duty

331
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:24,208
to protect everyone
who passes through here.

332
00:14:24,208 --> 00:14:27,000
even if they happen
to still be alive.

333
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,791
We're here.

334
00:14:33,916 --> 00:14:35,541
[sighing]

335
00:14:36,583 --> 00:14:38,000
We've waited long enough.

336
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Ah, maybe we should hit

337
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,041
all the other arcades
in the city.

338
00:14:42,041 --> 00:14:43,333
For Jay.

339
00:14:43,333 --> 00:14:45,791
Let's just go.

340
00:14:45,791 --> 00:14:48,166
[beeping and whooshing]

341
00:14:48,166 --> 00:14:49,625
Look!

342
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:53,291
Someone
is playing it remotely,

343
00:14:53,291 --> 00:14:55,208
which on an old-school cabinet
like this

344
00:14:55,208 --> 00:14:57,083
shouldn't be possible.

345
00:14:57,083 --> 00:14:58,041
That style...

346
00:14:58,041 --> 00:15:00,166
two blasts
after each rocket boost!

347
00:15:00,166 --> 00:15:03,083
Only one person
plays GX-P like that.

348
00:15:05,250 --> 00:15:07,916
So... you're not gonna say who?

349
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:12,791
What is this stuff?

350
00:15:12,791 --> 00:15:13,958
[Departed Soul] Don't ask me.

351
00:15:13,958 --> 00:15:16,583
Drinking it
is what helps souls move on,

352
00:15:16,583 --> 00:15:17,833
but for the living,

353
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,166
it can sometimes
provide healing.

354
00:15:20,166 --> 00:15:22,500
Your master will be pleased.

355
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:25,541
I don't think
my teacher does "pleased."

356
00:15:25,541 --> 00:15:27,875
Masters
can be tough sometimes.

357
00:15:27,875 --> 00:15:31,583
I had a... complicated
relationship with mine,

358
00:15:31,583 --> 00:15:32,875
and I betrayed him,

359
00:15:32,875 --> 00:15:34,541
my biggest regret.

360
00:15:34,541 --> 00:15:37,208
That's why I stay here
to help people.

361
00:15:37,208 --> 00:15:39,166
My master was wise.

362
00:15:39,166 --> 00:15:42,458
He taught me to defend those
who cannot defend themselves,

363
00:15:42,458 --> 00:15:44,500
so I honor his teachings

364
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:45,958
to make up for my mistakes.

365
00:15:45,958 --> 00:15:48,166
That's really... noble.

366
00:15:49,458 --> 00:15:51,166
[distant beasts screeching]

367
00:15:51,166 --> 00:15:54,041
Okay, now, let's get you
out of here.

368
00:15:55,875 --> 00:15:56,916
[game beeping and shuddering]

369
00:15:58,208 --> 00:15:59,750
Aw, come on.

370
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,958
I spent all day
rocking that high score!

371
00:16:01,958 --> 00:16:02,833
Now it's about to--

372
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,291
No! [sobbing]

373
00:16:07,875 --> 00:16:09,125
[Nya] "Jay"!

374
00:16:09,125 --> 00:16:11,500
It's really him.

375
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:18,166
We get you across the border,

376
00:16:18,166 --> 00:16:20,083
and the Soul-Suckers
can't follow you.

377
00:16:20,083 --> 00:16:21,833
I don't know how to thank you.

378
00:16:21,833 --> 00:16:23,333
Just stay alive.

379
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:24,333
Aah!

380
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:28,125
H'ah!

381
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,666
[distant snarling]

382
00:16:38,125 --> 00:16:39,875
[shouting] Ah!

383
00:16:39,875 --> 00:16:42,708
Ah... the elixir.

384
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:48,125
[groaning]

385
00:16:48,958 --> 00:16:49,916
Run!

386
00:16:49,916 --> 00:16:51,958
Get out of the Spectral Lands!

387
00:16:51,958 --> 00:16:53,250
I'm not leaving you!

388
00:16:59,875 --> 00:17:01,291
Ras! No!

389
00:17:03,583 --> 00:17:06,666
[gasping and groaning]

390
00:17:19,125 --> 00:17:21,000
[Ras groaning]

391
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:23,291
Come on, Ras, don't die on me.

392
00:17:26,666 --> 00:17:28,500
The elixir
from the Well of the Lost

393
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,625
can take time to work,

394
00:17:29,625 --> 00:17:31,625
but it's always effective.

395
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:32,666
Your master?

396
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,583
He's... my teacher.

397
00:17:36,583 --> 00:17:37,958
Looks like he taught you well.

398
00:17:37,958 --> 00:17:39,291
Thank you for everything.

399
00:17:39,291 --> 00:17:40,666
I wish I could repay you.

400
00:17:40,666 --> 00:17:43,750
You know, you could do
one thing for me.

401
00:17:43,750 --> 00:17:47,000
If you ever run into my master,
let him know...

402
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,541
he was right.

403
00:17:48,541 --> 00:17:49,541
Of course.

404
00:17:49,541 --> 00:17:50,500
Who was your master?

405
00:17:50,500 --> 00:17:52,041
His name is Wu.

406
00:17:52,041 --> 00:17:53,708
Master Wu?

407
00:17:53,708 --> 00:17:54,666
But...

408
00:17:54,666 --> 00:17:56,041
but he's dead.

409
00:17:56,041 --> 00:17:57,791
No, he must be alive.

410
00:17:57,791 --> 00:17:59,708
If he had departed, I'd know.

411
00:17:59,708 --> 00:18:01,000
He would have
come through here.

412
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,250
[distant beasts screeching]

413
00:18:03,916 --> 00:18:06,416
Now it's really time
for you to go.

414
00:18:07,208 --> 00:18:08,250
[unsheathing weapon]

415
00:18:10,375 --> 00:18:12,500
You're wrong, Ras.

416
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:15,583
The word "hero"
isn't meaningless.

417
00:18:15,583 --> 00:18:16,916
[beasts screeching]

418
00:18:16,916 --> 00:18:20,583
Sometimes it's
the only word that fits.

419
00:18:29,958 --> 00:18:31,875
More travelers?

420
00:18:33,875 --> 00:18:35,791
How can we be
of service to you?

421
00:18:38,291 --> 00:18:39,708
[Rox] Find it!

422
00:18:40,708 --> 00:18:42,708
[villagers screaming]

423
00:18:53,416 --> 00:18:56,625
There's no reason
to do this to our home!

424
00:18:56,625 --> 00:18:58,750
We will help you
with anything you need.

425
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,166
[explosion]

426
00:19:09,666 --> 00:19:12,083
That's it.

427
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:25,625
[Thunderfang] On time.

428
00:19:25,625 --> 00:19:28,583
Right when I expected.

429
00:19:28,583 --> 00:19:30,458
How could you know
we were coming?

430
00:19:30,458 --> 00:19:32,916
You still haven't
figured it out,

431
00:19:32,916 --> 00:19:35,416
Rox of the Wyldness?

432
00:19:35,416 --> 00:19:37,125
Everything you've ever done

433
00:19:37,125 --> 00:19:39,958
has been according to my plan.

434
00:19:39,958 --> 00:19:41,250
You lie.

435
00:19:41,250 --> 00:19:44,083
You've been chained down here
for millennia,

436
00:19:44,083 --> 00:19:45,375
helpless,

437
00:19:45,375 --> 00:19:48,500
but we have
a deal to make with you.

438
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,750
[cackling menacingly]

439
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:50,791
The ego...

440
00:19:50,791 --> 00:19:52,375
The entitlement!

441
00:19:52,375 --> 00:19:55,125
You remind me of my young self.

442
00:19:55,125 --> 00:19:56,750
Let me guess,

443
00:19:56,750 --> 00:19:58,083
this deal of yours

444
00:19:58,083 --> 00:20:00,041
is to free me of my chains,

445
00:20:00,041 --> 00:20:03,750
and I give you even more
of my power, yes?

446
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:04,625
Yes.

447
00:20:04,625 --> 00:20:06,250
What you call "a deal"

448
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:08,916
has always been my plan.

449
00:20:08,916 --> 00:20:12,000
Why do you think
I chose to empower five of you

450
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,125
to begin with?

451
00:20:13,125 --> 00:20:16,458
I am held by five chains,

452
00:20:16,458 --> 00:20:21,250
chains that can only be cut
by five prismatic blades.

453
00:20:22,833 --> 00:20:24,708
You have been defeated.

454
00:20:24,708 --> 00:20:26,041
Humiliated.

455
00:20:26,041 --> 00:20:27,958
So have I.

456
00:20:27,958 --> 00:20:30,083
You crave more power

457
00:20:30,083 --> 00:20:31,958
to crush your enemies?

458
00:20:31,958 --> 00:20:34,416
So do I.

459
00:20:34,416 --> 00:20:37,416
Find the blades, set me free,

460
00:20:37,416 --> 00:20:42,250
and yes, I will grant you
the power you want.

461
00:20:42,250 --> 00:20:44,166
How can we find them?

462
00:20:44,166 --> 00:20:47,666
I'm certain this gem
will be most helpful

463
00:20:47,666 --> 00:20:49,125
in your quest.

464
00:20:56,750 --> 00:20:58,250
We don't want
any more trouble.

465
00:21:02,333 --> 00:21:03,875
[transforming]

466
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:13,333
[grunting and straining]

467
00:21:15,541 --> 00:21:17,083
[all screaming]

468
00:21:25,250 --> 00:21:27,125
[grunting and snarling]

469
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

